From: uf maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Give Node pathToFileURL its URL return type

Issue: https://github.com/ubugeeei-prod/uf/issues/1451
Upstream: not filed yet
Submodule: 81b0c2a3dd591c66c51167aac341d851932bd9c5

Node's pathToFileURL returns a URL instance, whose href is always a string.
The legacy url$urlObject shape describes parsed URLs and makes href optional,
so valid callers fail type checking. `fileURLToPath` also accepts the returned
URL. Keep the optional shape for legacy parse/format callers.
Regression: crates/uf_check/tests/node_url.rs

diff --git a/evals/flow-typed/environment/node.js b/evals/flow-typed/environment/node.js
index 8f71a6a48..9895207a9 100644
--- a/evals/flow-typed/environment/node.js
+++ b/evals/flow-typed/environment/node.js
@@ -2589,4 +2589,4 @@ declare module "url" {
   declare function domainToUnicode(domain: string): string;
-  declare function pathToFileURL(path: string): url$urlObject;
-  declare function fileURLToPath(path: url$urlObject | string): string;
+  declare function pathToFileURL(path: string): URL;
+  declare function fileURLToPath(path: URL | url$urlObject | string): string;
   declare class URLSearchParams {
